    "probe_text": "The trace is confirmed against the source. Here is the complete ordered list of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Preconditions (before the controller body runs)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN`, else 403.\n2. **DTO Bean Validation** \u2014 the body is `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`. These annotations are checked before `addOwner` executes; any failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words, sep by space/`'`/`-`)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, trailing `.` allowed)\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (optional)\n\nNote: validation is against the **DTO**, not the JPA `Owner` entity. The entity's own constraints (`@NotEmpty` on names/address/city, `@Pattern` E.164 on telephone) only matter at persist time, and the controller normalizes values to satisfy them.\n\n## Inside `addOwner` \u2014 in execution order\n\n**Validations (each throws \u2192 the noted HTTP status):**\n\n3. `rejectMissingOrBlankFields` \u2014 after address normalization, if firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone is null or blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**.\n4. `rejectCityAtCapacity` \u2014 if the city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n5. `normalizeTelephone` \u2014 must resolve to `+` and 8\u201315 digits, and pass per-country national-length rules (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 else `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400**.\n6. `normalizeEmail` \u2014 if present, must match email regex and not be a disposable domain (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 else `InvalidEmailException` \u2192 **400**.\n7. `validatePostcode` \u2014 if present, must be 4 digits and fall in the city's region range (Sydney/NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne/VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane/QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**.\n8. `rejectDuplicateIdentity` \u2014 scans all owners: duplicate normalized telephone \u2192 `DuplicateTelephoneException` (**409**); duplicate email \u2192 `DuplicateEmailException` (**409**); duplicate householdId (unless `sharesHousehold=true`) \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` (**409**).\n9. `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` \u2014 supplied registrationDate after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**.\n10. `rejectDailyOwnerLimit` \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already carry the effective registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n**Side-effects (field derivations, all mutating the `Owner` before save):**\n\n11. `setAddress` \u2014 normalized address (trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, street abbreviations expanded).\n12. `setTelephone` \u2014 normalized E.164 telephone.\n13. `setEmail` \u2014 normalized (lower-cased) email, or null.\n14. `setRegistrationDate` \u2014 effective date (supplied or `now()`), rolled forward off weekends to the next business day.\n15. `setBulkSignupWarning` \u2014 true if > 80 owners already share that registration date.\n16. `setCustomerCode` \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; hash of telephone+lastName).\n17. `setMembershipNumber` \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<YY>`.\n18. `setHouseholdId` \u2014 12-char SHA-256 prefix of lastName+postcode.\n19. `setNamesakeCount` \u2014 count of existing owners with same first+last name.\n20. `setHouseholdMemberCount` \u2014 1 + existing owners sharing the householdId.\n21. `setMembershipPoints` \u2014 computed (email +2, unique name +1, household \u22653 +2, tenure \u2014 0 on create).\n22. `setMembershipLevel` \u2014 tier derived from points.\n23. `setPossibleDuplicate` / `setPossibleDuplicateOf` \u2014 soft-duplicate detection (same lastName+postcode, different telephone).\n\n**Persistence and terminal side-effects:**\n\n24. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 `@Transactional` DB insert via the repository.\n25. **AUDIT log** \u2014 a dedicated `\"AUDIT\"` logger emits `owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026`.\n26. Maps entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`, sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, returns **201 Created**.\n\n## Not present\n\nNo entity lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist` etc.), no Spring events/listeners, no `ApplicationEventPublisher`, and **no password encoding or email/message sending** anywhere in this path. All derivation is done imperatively in the controller. The only true external side-effects are the DB insert and the audit log line.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: several of the checks (city capacity, duplicate identity, namesake/household counts, daily limit, soft-duplicate) each independently call `findAllOwners()` \u2014 the full owner table is loaded from the DB multiple times per single create."
